    "body": "I can't get my head around the step 3 of [Initializing a new Document object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#initialise-the-document-object) by the way. It says:\r\n> If browsingContext's only entry in its session history is the about:blank Document that was added when browsingContext was created, and navigation is occurring with replacement enabled, and that Document has the same origin as the new Document, then set window to the Window object of that Document, and set settingsObject to window's relevant settings object.\r\n\r\nHow can the Document that is the only entry and the initial Document have the same origin as the new Document? Isn't the intial about:blank Document's origin of a top-level browsing context always an opaque origin?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
