    "created_at": "2020-12-01T21:53:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-01T22:02:19Z",
    "body": "Interesting, so I originally thought that even if we pass the right URL in \"early\" enough so that Window can be setup without referencing its not-yet-set `associated document`, then we'd still have another issue: [#concept-document-window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#concept-document-window) mentions that the Window's `associated document` is set when the Window is created, when it actually isn't. But now I'm confused about that.\r\n\r\nIn [#creating-a-new-browsing-context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#creating-a-new-browsing-context) in between steps 7 & 8, does the Window have an `associated document`? I guess it gets implicitly \"set\" by virtue of the Window being constructed? This implicitly-set document will have the `about:blank` URL as per DOM. Even then, we still have another issue:\r\n\r\n[#concept-document-window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#concept-document-window) mentions that the Window's `associated document` is *only* set once, that is, when navigating from the initial about:blank document to the document that the Window will carry \"forever\" I guess. However it is in fact set twice:\r\n 1. In #create-a-new-browsing-context step 15 when we call \"Set the active document of browsingContext to document\"\r\n    - I believe this is where we set the Window's `associated document` from the implicitly-created document mentioned in the second paragraph of this comment, to the explicitly-created about:blank document created in #creating-a-new-browsing-context step 13, which is weird because if my logic is right, then technically two about:blank documents get created per BC\r\n 1. In [history traversals](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#history-traversal:set-the-active-document)\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nHowever if Window's `associated document` is _not_ implicitly created by virtue of the Window being constructed, then what is Window's `associated document` by the time Window is constructed? It can't be null, because the spec says the member is a Document, not \"a Document or null\", so is it just a weird un-initialized Document? If that's the case, that's why I was thinking it seemed reasonable to let the Window \"constructor\" know how to create its `associated document` so they could be created simultaneously, thus making the text in [#concept-document-window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#concept-document-window) more accurate?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
